[Formspree](https://formspree.io) is a form backend. You point a form at a Formspree form, and Formspree receives and stores the submissions, so a static site can collect data without a server of its own. Its React library, `@formspree/react`, submits a form from a React component and reports the submission state.

# How does the integration work?

[Appwrite Sites](/docs/products/sites) has a **Job applications form with Formspree** template: a React, Vite, and Tailwind CSS job application form that sends every submission to Formspree. The form calls `useForm` from `@formspree/react` with the form ID in the `VITE_FORMSPREE_FORM_ID` environment variable, disables the submit button while sending, and shows a confirmation message when Formspree accepts the submission.

Appwrite builds the template from the [appwrite/templates-for-sites](https://github.com/appwrite/templates-for-sites/tree/main/react/formspree) repository and serves it as a static site:

| Setting | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Framework | React |
| Install command | `npm install` |
| Build command | `npm run build` |
| Output directory | `./dist` |
| Rendering | Static, with `index.html` as the fallback file |

{% info title="Self-hosted Appwrite" %}
The template builds on the `node-22` runtime, which `_APP_SITES_RUNTIMES` enables by default. To create a repository from the template, configure [version control](/docs/advanced/self-hosting/configuration/version-control) for your instance first. **Connect later** deploys the template straight from its public GitHub source.
{% /info %}

# How to implement

To collect job applications with Formspree and Appwrite Sites, there are several steps you must complete:

## Step 1: Create a form on Formspree

[Sign up for Formspree](https://formspree.io) and create a new form in the dashboard. Open the form's **Integration** tab and copy the hashid at the end of the URL shown under **Your form's endpoint is**. This is the form ID the template needs, for example `xrgkpqld`.

## Step 2: Create a site from the template

For this step, you must [create an account on Appwrite Cloud](/sign-up) or [self-host Appwrite](/docs/advanced/self-hosting) if you haven't already. In your Appwrite project, go to **Sites** and click **Create site**. Search the templates for **Job applications form with Formspree** and select it.

Enter a **Site name** and a **Site ID**, then choose **Connect your repository** if you want to edit the form later, or **Connect later** to deploy it as it is. Under the template's variables, set `VITE_FORMSPREE_FORM_ID` to the form ID you copied. The variable is required, and Vite reads it at build time, so the deployed form already points at your Formspree form.

Pick a subdomain under **Domain** and click **Deploy**.

## Step 3: Test the form

Open the deployed site, fill in the application, and click **Submit Application**. After Formspree accepts it, the page shows a thank-you message, and the submission appears in your form on the Formspree dashboard.

If you change the form ID later, update `VITE_FORMSPREE_FORM_ID` in the site's **Settings** > **Environment variables** and redeploy the site, because variable changes only apply to new deployments.

## Step 4: Customize the fields

The form lives in `src/App.jsx`. Each input's `name` attribute, such as `email`, `previous-company`, or `start-date`, becomes a field in the Formspree submission. Add, remove, or rename inputs there, and edit the options of the `position` select to list your open roles. Push the change to the production branch to redeploy.

